    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required deriving a `locality` region field on the owner from its city (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD; otherwise `UNKNOWN`), exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nI made two minimal edits, keeping structural impact low:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto` that looks the city up in an inline fixed table (`Map.of(...).getOrDefault(city, \"UNKNOWN\")`), matching the existing derived-field idiom (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.) already in that method.\n\nOnly 2 files touched, no new classes, no change to any method's cyclomatic complexity (the derivation is a self-contained expression rather than added control flow), and the surrounding classes were left untouched.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.",
